div.p:
With regard to the Bank we are seeking: 
                        —

a greater focus on the 15 debtor countries;
                        —

a major expansion of structural and sector adjustment lending where
                            there is a demand from countries;
                        —

more of the Bank’s lending program should be tranched in order to
                            monitor performance better;
                        —

a relaxation of the portfolio concentration guidelines for selected
                            debtor countries;
                        —

an improvement in the pace of internal procedures for processing loans
                            without sacrificing loan quality;


                        —

increased and continued coordination and cooperation with the IMF and with regional MDBs;
                        —

a stronger push by the Bank to get major debtor countries to move
                            toward market oriented economic policies, i.e. fair but strong
                            conditionality which will not be compromised;
                        —

suspension of lending for non-performance of lending conditions;
                            and
                        —

strengthened Bank staff for handling this type of lending.
